`flex` is declared `flex float`, so whether a root node asked for a share of
its parent is a numeric question. html answers it by handing the page the
viewport -- `html, body { height: 100% }` and a flex column body -- because a
root has no parent to take a share from.

Three pages say the three answers apart. `one` asks for a share and gets the
viewport. `zero` asks for none and must not: turning the viewport rule on for
a page that wants document flow changes how every page in it lays out.
`plain` writes no style at all, which is the same claim reached by a different
route -- the inliner binds the omitted prop to `Style`'s declared defaults, so
the node carries a `flex` field of 0 rather than no field, and a page that
never mentioned flex must read the same as one that set it to zero.

deny out/none/html/zero.html `(?m)^html, body \{ height: 100%; \}` -- flex = 0 asks for no share, so the page keeps document flow
deny out/none/html/zero.html `(?m)^body \{ display: flex` -- same rule, the other half of it
deny out/none/html/plain.html `(?m)^html, body \{ height: 100%; \}` -- a style nobody wrote asks for no share either
deny out/none/html/plain.html `(?m)^body \{ display: flex` -- same rule, the other half of it

-- site.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output { none { html } }

window #one(title="One", href="/one.html") {
    vbox(style=Style{flex=1.0}) {
        text(value="share")
    }
}

window #zero(title="Zero", href="/zero.html") {
    vbox(style=Style{flex=0.0}) {
        text(value="none")
    }
}

window #plain(title="Plain", href="/plain.html") {
    vbox {
        text(value="unsaid")
    }
}
-- out/none/html/one.html --
<!-- Code generated by sngl (html) from site.sngl; DO NOT EDIT. -->

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html><head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>One</title>
  <style>
* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
html, body { height: 100%; }
body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  </style>
</head><body>

<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1">
  <span>share</span>
</div>

<script>
(() => {
  // sngl-entry.js
  var state = {};
})();
</script>
</body></html>
